@media(max-width:850px){.sidebar{width:66px;padding:20px 9px 12px}.brand{padding:0 10px 38px}.brand-name,.side-label,.nav-link:not(.active)::first-letter,.nav-link{font-size:0}.nav-link{justify-content:center;padding:0}.nav-icon{font-size:17px}.nav-link.active{font-size:0}.nav-count,.nav-dot,.template-card,.sidebar-bottom .sync-card,.version,.profile span{display:none}.sidebar-bottom{display:flex;justify-content:center}.profile{border:0;padding:0;margin:0}.main-area{margin-left:66px;width:calc(100% - 66px)}.welcome-art{right:-105px;opacity:.7}.topbar{padding:0 20px}.page-wrap{padding:26px 20px}.builder-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.preview-column{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.preview-panel{grid-row:span 2}.content-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}}
-----
@media(max-width:600px){.topbar{height:55px;padding:0 12px}.breadcrumbs{gap:6px;font-size:9px}.draft-pill,.save-button{display:none}.top-actions{gap:6px}.export-button{height:31px;padding:0 9px;font-size:9px}.page-wrap{padding:22px 13px}.welcome-row{min-height:144px}.welcome-row h1,.subpage-head h1{font-size:25px}.welcome-copy{max-width:245px;line-height:1.5}.welcome-art{width:220px;right:-97px;top:3px;opacity:.45}.project-strip{margin-top:0;padding:0 9px;gap:8px;height:59px}.project-glyph{width:29px;height:29px}.project-input-wrap{width:140px}.strip-divider{margin:0 1px}.project-meta{display:none}.section-heading{align-items:flex-start}.section-heading h2{font-size:15px}.builder-panel{padding:14px 11px}.panel-step{font-size:7px}.type-option{padding:0 5px;gap:5px}.type-option small{font-size:7px}.type-icon{width:23px;height:23px}.field-row{gap:8px}.field label{font-size:7px}.field input,.id-input,.select-wrap select{font-size:9px}.behavior-options{grid-template-columns:1fr}.behavior-toggle{height:38px;padding:0 9px}.behavior-toggle b{font-size:9px}.behavior-toggle small{font-size:8px}.behavior-toggle .toggle-ui{margin-left:auto}.preview-column{grid-template-columns:1fr}.preview-panel{grid-row:auto}.tip-card{display:none}.content-toolbar{flex-wrap:wrap;gap:7px}.search-box{width:100%}.filter-tabs{order:2;overflow:auto;width:100%}.filter-tab{padding:7px 8px;white-space:nowrap}.secondary-button{margin-left:auto}.content-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.files-layout{grid-template-columns:1fr}.file-tree{min-height:170px}.subpage-head{align-items:flex-start;gap:10px}.subpage-head .export-button{white-space:nowrap;margin-top:20px}.footer{padding:13px;gap:10px;font-size:7px;flex-wrap:wrap}.footer>span:last-child{margin-left:auto}.content-card{padding:9px}.card-art{height:58px}.modal{padding:21px}.footer{margin-top:5px}}
-----

At <=850, builder-grid is 1fr; page-wrap width 324 at 390 (390-66), padding 20 -> 284 content. At <=600, padding 13 -> 298 content. Why builder-panel width 372? Because the viewport becomes wider due to horizontal overflow from welcome-art? CSS grid container width maybe min-content forced by `.type-picker` and `.behavior-toggle` white-space nowrap, causing min-width 372. The grid item has min-width auto, and its content min width (behavior toggles with small white-space nowrap at 3 columns before media 600 changed to 1fr; but our appended @media 600 sets behavior-options 1fr, yet the original @media 600 also 1fr. Still button content maybe type-picker: 3 columns each min-content; .type-option small white-space nowrap makes min width; total 348. Need min-width:0 on grid items and allow text ellipsis/wrap.

Root cause: `.builder-grid` grid item's min width expands; `.field-row` 2 columns with labels/inputs min-content; `.type-picker` 3 columns. To make mobile fit, set `.builder-grid{min-width:0}`, `.builder-grid>*{min-width:0}`, `.builder-panel{min-width:0}`, `.field-row{grid-template-columns:1fr}` on mobile, `.type-picker{grid-template-columns:1fr}` or allow small. Also `.type-option small` hidden at <=600 to reduce. `.panel-step` perhaps hide. `.behavior-toggle small` might be long; 1fr width 298 and nowrap small could be ~? 103px. Fine.

The horizontal overflow from welcome-art also causes scroll width to 494. `welcome-row` has `overflow:hidden`, but welcome-art is inside welcome-row? Wait welcome-row overflow hidden, so art shouldn't extend scroll? It has overflow:hidden but absolute children could still show? In CSS, overflow hidden clips. The wide element detection includes off-screen elements but they may be clipped and not contribute to scroll width? Scroll width 451 corresponds builder-panel right 451, not art 494. So builder panel is main cause. The welcome-art clipping might not add scroll.

Fix mobile:
```
@media(max-width:600px){
 .builder-grid,.builder-grid>*{min-width:0}
 .field-row{grid-template-columns:1fr}
 .type-picker{grid-template-columns:1fr} /* or perhaps 3 but min compact */
 .type-option{min-width:0;height:50px}
 .type-option small{display:none}
 .panel-step{display:none}
 .behavior-toggle b, small {white-space:normal}
 .preview-column{min-width:0}
}
```
But 3 type options in a row is nicer for mobile. Each width ~90; currently min-content 102 due to texts. Hide small and reduce padding => fit. Type-picker can stay 3 cols; set `.type-option{min-width:0}` and `.type-option span:last-child{min-width:0}`? The b "Criatura" ~44px plus icon 23 + gaps/padding = ~86; 3*86=258 plus gaps 14 = 272 < 298. Good. Hide small. Also `white-space:nowrap` on b? none. fine.

