Now dedupe key and name repetition. 
Dedupe:
```
const key = entry.type + '|' + entry.kind + '|' + cleanText(entry.clause, 120).toLowerCase();
```
But when wantsArsenal extras all have clause=text, so same type/kind but different kinds anyway. If two identical default extras? no. If detected has duplicate identical clauses, dedupe.

Name repetition in buildLocalSpec:
```
let noun = nounFor(...)
let of = theme.of;
if (slugify(noun) === slugify(theme.label)) {
  if (type==='block') noun='Bloque';
  else if (type==='entity') noun='Criatura';
  else if (kind==='food') noun='Alimento';
  else if (kind==='gem') noun='Gema';
  else noun='Reliquia'; // weapons? "Espada de espada" impossible
}
```
But "Piedra de piedra" -> block -> Bloque de piedra. "Amatista de amatista" -> Gema de amatista. Good. For "Cristal de vacío", noun "Cristal" != "vacío". Fine.
Also if explicitName given, no change.

Need to know `theme.of` for theme. Good.

Let's edit.

